<title>UK: UK April natural gas output falls 12 pct - Wood Mac.</title>
<headline>UK April natural gas output falls 12 pct - Wood Mac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK natural gas production averaged 8,639 million cubic feet a day (mmcfd) in April, consultants Wood Mackenzie said in June's North Sea Report published on Monday.</p>
<p>This represented a drop of 12 percent on the March figure of 9,802 mmcfd, but was up by 8 percent from the previous April, when output reached 7,990 mmcfd.</p>
<p>The seasonal change was reflected in Morecambe production, which fell by 42 percent to 673 mmcfd in April, a decline of 505 mmcfd from March.</p>
<p>Sean, Welland and Trent all had zero nominations in April, and other big falls were seen at Leman (down 292 mmcfd), Hewett (down 139 mmcfd), Lomond (down 71 mmcfd) and Cleeton (down 49 mmcfd).</p>
